#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:5
#: 6c444a9c3e7d474887184e03549c63b7
msgid "Analog Current Monitor Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:7
#: ab6921f959b245a5898433d066935d19
msgid "Analog current monitors usually consist of an ultralow resistance shunt used to generate a very small voltage which is then electronically amplified and delivered to the autopilot via one of its analog-to-digital (A/D) interfaces. In ArduPilot, this voltage is scaled by the :ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` parameter to indicated the current level. The :ref:`BATT_AMP_OFFSET<BATT_AMP_OFFSET__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` parameter is provided to correct for any voltage offsets generated by the current monitor's amplifier that results in output when zero current is flowing thru the shunt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:12
#: 185d5924ecbe49849d64b9839f731fe3
msgid "This monitor's accuracy  and repeatability across different boards is dependent on many factors: - The tolerance of the shunt resistor and amplifier components - The quality of the PCB layout which can induce parasitic errors due to high current flows - The temperature coefficient of the components since high currents can cause localized heating in some cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:17
#: cafccfe0c08c40eebfa1cb11bcae1b24
msgid "many of these issues do not occur if using a HALL-EFFECT current sensor instead of a resistive shunt. Unfortunately, those are more bulky and expensive and are not practical for use on autopilots with integrated current sensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:19
#: fc28533d20a540c3a5af5dad60a9c330
msgid "The net result is that shunt current sensors usually need their ArduPilot parameters tweaked to achieve good results. There are two main methods for calibration: #. Using a good ammeter. Hobby grade devices such as the `GT Power Meter <https://www.amazon.com/GT-Power-Analyzer-Consumption-Performance/dp/B00C1BZSYO>`__ or inexpensive `DVM types <https://www.amazon.com/GT-Power-Analyzer-Consumption-Performance/dp/B00C1BZSYO>`__ can be used to set the scale and offset. #. Empirically, by test flying and comparing the used mah reported for the flight vs how much charge is put back into the battery during recharge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:24
#: 7d7007a1df90464395e7e8d00296d224
msgid "Using an Ammeter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:25
#: 6b4966e22f5b49cab464f36e79a48cda
msgid "Attach the ammeter and power the vehicle with its battery. Connect to the GCS and note the current reported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:26
#: 44402286b8a24ee192b9b59eea31dd25
msgid "Adjust the :ref:`BATT_AMP_OFFSET<BATT_AMP_OFFSET__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` parameter to match the ammeter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:27
#: ac1dfacab3984e3cbd97fcc679e3f539
msgid "Arm and throttle up the vehicle. For Copters this can be done with the propellers reversed to hold the vehicle down. For Plane, it should be secured (A helper is advised) to prevent movement. Rover will need some way to load the wheels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:29
#: 38b460d6dbba459794310625e8a92a1f
msgid "be safe! make sure you or someone else cannot be injured while doing this!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:31
#: c41bae8c5f364be5aa409d458f8aff55
msgid "The throttle level should stimulate current consumption close to the expected normal vehicle flight condition (ie like cruising level in Plane or hovering in Copter)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:32
#: 33a98b54d3ec469abd1245b4d5ba3a15
msgid "Note the difference between the ammeter and what the GCS reports and adjust the :ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` to match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:33
#: 64a22fb145034d14810507341082821b
msgid "Recheck the idle current and re-adjust the :ref:`BATT_AMP_OFFSET<BATT_AMP_OFFSET__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>`, if needed. There will be some interaction between it and the :ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` so some repetition of the above may be needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:35
#: 6fe0201ee3274c5e9d71fc4738439125
msgid "Its always good to use the process explained next to tweak the :ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` parameter after a real flight or two."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:38
#: d79aebc029e244ad9ae80f1f39b6075c
msgid "Empirical Adjustment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:39
#: 373d1dd3dd0a471384f8ff6077f8917b
msgid "Power the vehicle on the bench with its battery and note the reported current to the GCS. As a guess, normally it should read in the .2 to .4A range with the autopilot and peripherals powered. If a VTX is also in the system, it could be in the .6A range. Adjust :ref:`BATT_AMP_OFFSET<BATT_AMP_OFFSET__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` to get that reported value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:40
#: cee602ec0dc14f8d957c69e40ad64008
msgid "Test fly with a lengthy period in its normal flying condition (ie one takeoff, one landing only). Try to use at least 50% of the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:41
#: 6e738d4b52b149a0b6121854389713de
msgid "From the flight log determine how much battery was consumed, re-charge it and note how much was put back. This is usually about 105% of what was consumed. Adjust the :ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` param according to this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:43
#: e3d828b43a494b56a50548d0ac26d450
msgid "(amount of charge put back into battery/ reported used charge ) * current value becomes the new value for :ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:44
#: ff9bba87516b4731ad75588242e29022
msgid "Readjust the :ref:`BATT_AMP_OFFSET<BATT_AMP_OFFSET__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` value on the bench"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-current-calibration.rst:45
#: b8cddcc0796b4ad685f4b27f13a3e8b1
msgid "Test fly again, iterate as needed."
msgstr ""
